{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"In a U.S. ETF’s **primary market**, the fund (through its trust or service providers) may charge an authorized participant (AP) a **fixed transaction fee** and, where permitted, a **variable fee**:\n\n- **Fixed fee:** generally covers the fund’s routine costs of processing a creation or redemption—such as transfer-agent, custody, or operational expenses. It is typically charged per order, not necessarily equal to the fund’s actual cost.\n- **Variable fee:** generally offsets costs that vary with the basket or transaction, especially brokerage, taxes, market impact, and other trading costs. It can help protect existing shareholders from dilution.\n\nThe **AP pays the fund’s charge** when it submits the creation/redemption order. The AP may in turn pass costs along to its client or incorporate them into its quote; that is separate from the fund charge.\n\n**AP compensation is distinct:** an AP may earn a spread or other compensation from its client for arranging the transaction. Fund charges go to the fund or designated service provider; AP compensation goes to the AP. **Recipients can differ**, and the AP need not receive the fund’s fees. Actual fee terms and permitted charges depend on the ETF’s governing documents and disclosed schedule."}}
